WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.990
This one has more of a story.

2
00:00:03.990 --> 00:00:08.690
One day Pastor, who went to primary and secondary school

3
00:00:08.690 --> 00:00:12.780
with me, wrote to me and introduced me to Cesar and

4
00:00:12.780 --> 00:00:16.550
Alejandro to apply to a hackathon.

5
00:00:16.550 --> 00:00:21.930
They were one short, and he asked me if I would join

6
00:00:21.930 --> 00:00:23.060
them.

7
00:00:23.060 --> 00:00:24.080
The old Juan would have said no.

8
00:00:24.080 --> 00:00:28.030
The old Juan would have said no,

9
00:00:28.030 --> 00:00:31.060
maybe out of shyness or laziness,

10
00:00:31.060 --> 00:00:36.130
but this time I thought that the worst thing that could

11
00:00:36.130 --> 00:00:41.270
happen was not getting in, and at the very least we

12
00:00:41.270 --> 00:00:43.060
would learn a lot.

13
00:00:43.060 --> 00:00:50.460
We came up with several ideas, but the one that won was

14
00:00:50.460 --> 00:00:56.360
Tripealo, a marketplace for travel experiences in

15
00:00:56.360 --> 00:01:02.210
Venezuela, and out of a thousand people who applied,

16
00:01:02.210 --> 00:01:06.520
we were among the hundred who went to Yomis' offices in

17
00:01:06.520 --> 00:01:08.060
Caracas.

18
00:01:08.060 --> 00:01:13.290
We didn't win, but I heard many founders who now compete

19
00:01:13.290 --> 00:01:17.490
in Silicon Valley against the top companies in the

20
00:01:17.490 --> 00:01:22.620
United States, and we left with the push to keep going,

21
00:01:22.620 --> 00:01:24.060
and going.

22
00:01:24.060 --> 00:01:27.270
And they carried on with Tripealo,

23
00:01:27.270 --> 00:01:32.380
and I left to continue with my co-founder at Salvalo.

24
00:01:32.380 --> 00:01:37.450
Today, Tripealo and Salvalo are both running,

25
00:01:37.450 --> 00:01:44.780
and I'm all in on Salvalo in what I like to call founder

26
00:01:44.780 --> 00:01:45.690
mode.

27
00:01:45.690 --> 00:01:50.060
They're like my founder bros.

28
00:01:50.060 --> 00:01:54.060
We are together, but not mixed up.

29
00:01:54.060 --> 00:01:58.080
This hackathon was the turning point between the old

30
00:01:58.080 --> 00:02:02.220
Juan, like just a software developer,

31
00:02:02.220 --> 00:02:08.060
and the Juan of today, which is almost an entrepreneur.

32
00:02:08.060 --> 00:02:12.060
I'm really grateful for this experience,

33
00:02:12.060 --> 00:02:16.060
and I learned a lot from a lot of people,

34
00:02:16.060 --> 00:02:20.578
but a lot about myself.
